- risks: rendering combinators, original versus current revision confusion, implicit selection, advisory failures and tight unchanged payload budgets. Each has an explicit approved regression or qualification task. No second validator, registry, approval path or adapter policy is introduced.
- runtime/source drift: original root builds are not repaired. Canonical generation and dependency resolution are verified in the isolated candidate, then only reviewed owned outputs return. Existing native harness/task/audit fingerprints remain fixed.
- context_graph_impact: no new domain or ownership boundary; existing Core read contract remains owner. No automatic graph node.
- missing_evidence: implementation and fresh qualification evidence are pending tasks, not prior acceptance. Native execution waits for the build, model-free checks and protected preflight.
- required_next_step: record this analysis through step.record; continue the same Run, then execute the approved CD+Tests scope.
